    "question": "A 58-year-old female with BMI 42 kg/m² is referred to the Respiratory Clinic with chronic dyspnoea on exertion and poor sleep quality. Her partner reports loud snoring and witnessed apnoeas. Daytime arterial blood gas on room air shows: pH 7.38, PaCO2 52 mmHg, PaO2 64 mmHg, HCO3 30 mmol/L, BE +4. Overnight polysomnography reveals AHI 42 events/hour with oxygen desaturations to 72%. Spirometry shows FEV1/FVC 0.78 (predicted 0.75-0.85), FEV1 68% predicted. Which of the following statements regarding her diagnosis and management is MOST accurate?",
    "options": {
